[[8,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/3025001\">1016A10</a></p><p>1. Disconnect the pipe from its housing on the crankcase.</p><p>2. Disconnect the pipe from the cam cover.</p><p>3. Remove the engine oil vapour pipe.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2002376.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[8,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Fit the oil vapour pipe to the crankcase\nand cam cover fittings.</p><p>Secure the ends using collars.</p><p><a href=\"#/3025001\">1016A10</a></p>"]]